== a builtin name:
echo
== an absent name exits 1 with no output:
rc=1
== a program resolved in a temp PATH:
TMPDIR/mytool
== -a lists every match in the temp PATH:
TMPDIR/mytool
== -q on a resolving name is silent, status 0:
status=0
== -q on a missing name is silent, status 1:
status=1
== without -q the location still prints:
1
